IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- SCHEDULE 5, paragraphs A1 to 3B: pension increase or lump sum where entitlement to a Category A or
-- Category B retirement pension is deferred (the pensioner's own deferment).
-- The widowed person's paragraphs (3C to 9) are in ssc9-sch5-w.l4.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text, and nothing here
-- is "verified against the official text". The converter dropped the paragraph numbers of this Schedule;
-- every label below is the number an in-text citation gives (see NOTES.md, "Paragraph labels that are inferred").
-- Money is a NUMBER in pounds, a weekly figure unless its name says otherwise.
-- Every "no" branch carries FALSE-kind and every "not covered" branch NOTHING-kind (NOTES.md, Reading a result).

§ `Schedule 5 -- pension increase or lump sum where entitlement to retirement pension is deferred`

§§ `Paragraph A1 -- choice between increase of pension and lump sum`

-- A1(1)(a) and (b): the two things the person elects between.
DECLARE `sch 5 Election` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5 an election that paragraph 1 (the increase of pension) applies`
    `sch 5 an election that paragraph 3A (the lump sum) applies`

-- The parties and acts of the election duty (A1(1)): one party, one act that carries the choice made.
DECLARE `sch 5 Party` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5 the person whose entitlement is deferred`

DECLARE `sch 5 Act` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5 makes an election` HAS `the choice` IS A `sch 5 Election`

-- "at least 12 months": the period of deferment begins on its first day and the twelve months are complete
-- at the end of the day before the first anniversary. `add months` clamps 29 February to 28 February.
-- FORK (NOTES.md, F1): for a deferment that began on 29 February and a year with no 29 February, the text does not
-- say whether the twelve months are complete at the end of 27 February or of 28 February, so the one day on which
-- the two readings differ answers NOTHING.
-- src:5069 | (1) Where a person’s entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred and the period of deferment is at least 12 months, the person shall, on claiming his pension or within a prescribed period after claiming it, elect in the prescribed manner either—
@ref sch 5 para A1(1) (src:5069)
GIVEN `the period of deferment` IS A Period
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para A1(1) the period of deferment is at least 12 months` MEANS
    IF (DATE_MONTH first EQUALS 2) AND (DATE_DAY first EQUALS 29) AND (DATE_DAY anniversary EQUALS 28) AND ((Day last) EQUALS ((Day anniversary) MINUS 1))
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "at least 12 months" does not say what the twelve months from 29 February end on in a year without one
    ELSE JUST ((Day last) AT LEAST ((Day anniversary) MINUS 1))
    WHERE
        first MEANS `the period of deferment`'s `the first day`
        last MEANS `the period of deferment`'s `the last day`
        anniversary MEANS `add months` first 12

-- A1(1): the duty to elect. The conditions are introduced by "Where", which is not an "if": a person who is outside
-- them is not told "no" by this sub-paragraph, so the answer is NOTHING (paragraph 1(1)(a) deals with the short deferment).
-- src:5069 | (1) Where a person’s entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred and the period of deferment is at least 12 months, the person shall, on claiming his pension or within a prescribed period after claiming it, elect in the prescribed manner either—
-- src:5070 | (a) that paragraph 1 (entitlement to increase of pension) is to apply in relation to the period of deferment, or
-- src:5071 | (b) that paragraph 3A (entitlement to lump sum) is to apply in relation to the period of deferment.
@ref sch 5 para A1(1) (src:5069-5071)
GIVEN `the entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of deferment` IS A Period
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para A1(1) the person must elect` MEANS
    IF NOT `the entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a person’s entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred"
    ELSE CONSIDER `sch 5 para A1(1) the period of deferment is at least 12 months` `the period of deferment`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the 29 February fork of the 12 months
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and the period of deferment is at least 12 months"

-- A1(1) and (2) as a regulative rule: the person shall elect on claiming or within the prescribed period
-- after claiming it. The period is prescribed, so it is an input (days). If the period passes with no election,
-- A1(2) treats the person as having elected the lump sum: the duty is discharged by that deeming and
-- is not breached, so the lapse leads to FULFILLED (the deemed election is `sch 5 para A1(2) the election that is treated as made`).
-- The choice in the action is a wildcard: either election discharges the duty.
-- src:5069 | (1) Where a person’s entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred and the period of deferment is at least 12 months, the person shall, on claiming his pension or within a prescribed period after claiming it, elect in the prescribed manner either—
-- src:5070 | (a) that paragraph 1 (entitlement to increase of pension) is to apply in relation to the period of deferment, or
-- src:5071 | (b) that paragraph 3A (entitlement to lump sum) is to apply in relation to the period of deferment.
-- src:5072 | (2) If no election under sub-paragraph (1) is made within the period prescribed under that sub-paragraph, the person is to be treated as having made an election under sub-paragraph (1)(b).
@ref sch 5 para A1(1) and (2) (src:5069-5072)
GIVEN `the prescribed period after claiming, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 5 Party` `sch 5 Act`
`sch 5 para A1(1) the election duty` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 5 the person whose entitlement is deferred`
    MUST `sch 5 makes an election` choice
    WITHIN `the prescribed period after claiming, in days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

-- A1(2): if no election is made within the prescribed period the person is treated as having made the (b) election.
-- src:5072 | (2) If no election under sub-paragraph (1) is made within the period prescribed under that sub-paragraph, the person is to be treated as having made an election under sub-paragraph (1)(b).
@ref sch 5 para A1(2) (src:5072)
GIVEN `the election made within the prescribed period` IS A MAYBE `sch 5 Election`
GIVETH A `sch 5 Election`
`sch 5 para A1(2) the election that is treated as made` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the election made within the prescribed period`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `sch 5 an election that paragraph 3A (the lump sum) applies`
    WHEN JUST chosen THEN chosen

-- A1(3): regulations may allow a change of election and avoid duplication of payment: a regulation-making power,
-- inert (machinery) in NOTES.md.

-- A1(4): no election applies to so much of the pension as consists of an increase under paragraphs 5 to 6A.
-- src:5078 | (4) Where the Category A or Category B retirement pension includes any increase under paragraphs 5 to 6A, no election under sub-paragraph (1) applies to so much of the pension as consists of that increase (an entitlement to an increase of pension in respect of such an increase after a period of deferment being conferred either by paragraphs 1 and 2 or by paragraph 2A).
@ref sch 5 para A1(4) (src:5078)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the pension` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of the weekly rate that consists of an increase under paragraphs 5 to 6A` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para A1(4) the weekly rate to which an election applies` MEANS
    `the weekly rate of the pension` MINUS `the part of the weekly rate that consists of an increase under paragraphs 5 to 6A`   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no election under sub-paragraph (1) applies to so much of the pension as consists of that increase"

§§ `Paragraph 1 -- increase of pension where entitlement is deferred`

-- 1(1): applies where deferred and (a) the deferment is under 12 months or (b) an A1(1)(a) election was made.
-- "applies where" is not an "if": outside the two conditions the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:5080 | (1) This paragraph applies where a person’s entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred and one of the following conditions is met—
-- src:5081 | (a) the period of deferment is less than 12 months, or
-- src:5082 | (b) the person has made an election under paragraph A1(1)(a) in relation to the period of deferment.
@ref sch 5 para 1(1) (src:5080-5082)
GIVEN `the entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of deferment` IS A Period
      `the election made, or treated as made` IS A MAYBE `sch 5 Election`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 1(1) this paragraph applies` MEANS
    IF NOT `the entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph applies where a person’s entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred"
    ELSE CONSIDER `sch 5 para A1(1) the period of deferment is at least 12 months` `the period of deferment`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the 29 February fork of the 12 months
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE   -- limb (a): "the period of deferment is less than 12 months"
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             CONSIDER `the election made, or treated as made`
             WHEN JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 1 (the increase of pension) applies` THEN JUST TRUE   -- limb (b)
             WHEN JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 3A (the lump sum) applies` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): neither condition (a) nor (b) is met, and the sub-paragraph says only when it applies
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no election is recorded

-- 1(2): the increase is the aggregate of the increments, but only if that is at least 1 per cent of the rate.
-- "the rate of the pension" is read as the rate being increased, before this increase (NOTES.md, F2).
-- src:5083 | (2) The rate of the person’s Category A or Category B retirement pension shall be increased by an amount equal to the aggregate of the increments to which he is entitled under paragraph 2, but only if that amount is enough to increase the rate of the pension by at least 1 per cent.
@ref sch 5 para 1(2) (src:5083)
GIVEN `the aggregate of the increments under paragraph 2` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly rate of the pension before the increase` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 1(2) the amount by which the rate of the pension is increased` MEANS
    IF `the aggregate of the increments under paragraph 2` AT LEAST (`the weekly rate of the pension before the increase` DIVIDED BY 100)
    THEN `the aggregate of the increments under paragraph 2`
    ELSE 0   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but only if that amount is enough to increase the rate of the pension by at least 1 per cent"

§§ `Paragraph 2 -- increments`

-- 2(2): "incremental period" means any period of six days treated by regulations as days of increment.
-- The days of increment are a fact the regulations decide (an input). NOTES.md, F3: whether the six days must be
-- consecutive is not said; the reading taken counts six days of increment as one period wherever they fall.
-- src:5085 | (2) In this Schedule—
-- src:5086 | “incremental period” means any period of six days which are treated by regulations as days of increment for the purposes of this Schedule in relation to the person and the pension in question; ...
@ref sch 5 para 2(2) (src:5085-5086)
GIVEN `the number of days in the period of deferment that regulations treat as days of increment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 2(2) the number of complete incremental periods` MEANS
    FLOOR (`the number of days in the period of deferment that regulations treat as days of increment` DIVIDED BY 6)

-- 2(1): one increment for each complete incremental period.
-- src:5084 | (1) Subject to paragraph 3 below, a person is entitled to an increment under this paragraph for each complete incremental period in his period of deferment.
@ref sch 5 para 2(1) (src:5084)
GIVEN `the number of complete incremental periods` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 2(1) the number of increments` MEANS
    `the number of complete incremental periods`

-- 2(4): rounding of an amount calculated under 2(3).
-- src:5089 | (4) Where an amount is required to be calculated in accordance with the provisions of sub-paragraph (3) above—
-- src:5090 | (a) the amount so calculated shall be rounded to the nearest penny, taking any 1/2p as nearest to the next whole penny above; and
-- src:5091 | (b) where the amount so calculated would, apart from this sub-paragraph, be a sum less than 1/2p, that amount shall be taken to be zero, notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, the Pensions Act or the Administration Act.
@ref sch 5 para 2(4) (src:5089-5091)
GIVEN `the amount calculated under sub-paragraph (3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 2(4) the amount calculated under sub-paragraph (3) as rounded` MEANS
    IF `the amount calculated under sub-paragraph (3)` LESS THAN 0.005
    THEN 0   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that amount shall be taken to be zero, notwithstanding any other provision of this Act"
    ELSE (FLOOR ((`the amount calculated under sub-paragraph (3)` TIMES 100) PLUS 0.5)) DIVIDED BY 100

-- 2(3): the increment for one incremental period is 1/5th per cent of the weekly rate to which the person would have
-- been entitled had the entitlement not been deferred; 2(4) rounds it.
-- src:5088 | (3) Subject to paragraph 3 below, the amount of the increment for any such incremental period shall be 1/5th per cent of the weekly rate of the Category A or Category B retirement pension to which that person would have been entitled for the period if his entitlement had not been deferred.
@ref sch 5 para 2(3) (src:5088)
GIVEN `the weekly rate to which the person would have been entitled for the period if the entitlement had not been deferred` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 2(3) the increment for one incremental period` MEANS
    `sch 5 para 2(4) the amount calculated under sub-paragraph (3) as rounded` ((`the weekly rate to which the person would have been entitled for the period if the entitlement had not been deferred` DIVIDED BY 5) DIVIDED BY 100)

-- Paragraph 2 as a whole: the aggregate of the increments for the complete incremental periods.
-- src:5084 | (1) Subject to paragraph 3 below, a person is entitled to an increment under this paragraph for each complete incremental period in his period of deferment.
-- src:5085 | (2) In this Schedule—
-- src:5086 | “incremental period” means any period of six days which are treated by regulations as days of increment for the purposes of this Schedule in relation to the person and the pension in question; ...
-- src:5088 | (3) Subject to paragraph 3 below, the amount of the increment for any such incremental period shall be 1/5th per cent of the weekly rate of the Category A or Category B retirement pension to which that person would have been entitled for the period if his entitlement had not been deferred.
@ref sch 5 para 2 (src:5084-5088)
GIVEN `the weekly rate to which the person would have been entitled for the period if the entitlement had not been deferred` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days in the period of deferment that regulations treat as days of increment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 2 the aggregate of the increments` MEANS
    (`sch 5 para 2(1) the number of increments` (`sch 5 para 2(2) the number of complete incremental periods` `the number of days in the period of deferment that regulations treat as days of increment`))
    TIMES (`sch 5 para 2(3) the increment for one incremental period` `the weekly rate to which the person would have been entitled for the period if the entitlement had not been deferred`)

-- 2(5) to (6): what the weekly rate of pension counts. The record holds the weekly rate as the sum of the pension
-- apart from the increases the sub-paragraph names, and each increase it names.
DECLARE `sch 5 Weekly pension` HAS
    `the pension apart from the increases named in this Schedule` IS A NUMBER
    `the increase under section 47(1)`                             IS A NUMBER   -- as 2(6) reads it: s 47(2) and s 46(5) of the Pensions Act disregarded
    `the increase under paragraph 4`                               IS A NUMBER
    `the increases under paragraphs 5 to 6A`                       IS A NUMBER
    `the increase under section 83A`                               IS A NUMBER
    `the increase under section 85`                                IS A NUMBER
    `the graduated retirement benefit`                             IS A NUMBER

-- src:5092 | (5) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (3) above the weekly rate of pension for any period shall be taken—
-- src:5093 | (a) to include any increase under section 47(1) above and any increase under paragraph 4, 5, 5A, 6 or 6A below, but
-- src:5094 | (b) not to include any increase under section ... 83A or 85 above or any graduated retirement benefit.
@ref sch 5 para 2(5) (src:5092-5094)
GIVEN pension IS A `sch 5 Weekly pension`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 2(5) the weekly rate of pension for sub-paragraph (3)` MEANS
    pension's `the pension apart from the increases named in this Schedule`
    PLUS pension's `the increase under section 47(1)`
    PLUS pension's `the increase under paragraph 4`
    PLUS pension's `the increases under paragraphs 5 to 6A`
    -- left out, each by a flat negative: "not to include any increase under section ... 83A or 85 above or any graduated retirement benefit"
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not to include any increase under section ... 83A or 85 above or any graduated retirement benefit"

-- 2(6): the section 47(1) increase for this purpose is the one that would take place if section 47(2) of this Act
-- (the deduction for additional pension) and section 46(5) of the Pensions Act were disregarded.
-- src:5095 | (6) The reference in sub-paragraph (5) above to any increase under subsection (1) of section 47 above shall be taken as a reference to any increase that would take place under that subsection if subsection (2) of that section and section 46(5) of the Pensions Act were disregarded.
@ref sch 5 para 2(6) (src:5095)
GIVEN `the increase under section 47(1) before the deduction under section 47(2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the increase under section 47(1) actually payable after that deduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 2(6) the increase under section 47(1) that is counted` MEANS
    `the increase under section 47(1) before the deduction under section 47(2)`

-- 2(7): an uprating order that came into force during the deferment is treated as in force from before it began.
-- src:5096 | (7) Where one or more orders have come into force under section 150 or 150A of the Administration Act during the period of deferment, the rate for any incremental period shall be determined as if the order or orders had come into force before the beginning of the period of deferment.
@ref sch 5 para 2(7) (src:5096)
GIVEN `an order under section 150 or 150A of the Administration Act came into force during the period of deferment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weekly rate at the beginning of the period of deferment` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly rate as it would be had the order or orders come into force before the beginning of the period of deferment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para 2(7) the rate for an incremental period` MEANS
    IF `an order under section 150 or 150A of the Administration Act came into force during the period of deferment`
    THEN JUST `the weekly rate as it would be had the order or orders come into force before the beginning of the period of deferment`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where one or more orders have come into force ... during the period of deferment"

-- 2(8): after a pensioner's rights premium is paid, a guaranteed minimum pension connected with the employment to
-- which the premium relates is disregarded in calculating increments falling to be paid after the premium date.
-- src:5097 | (8) Where a pensioner’s rights premium is paid in respect of a person who is, or if his entitlement had not been deferred would be, entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension, then, in calculating any increment under this paragraph which falls to be paid to him in respect of such a pension after the date on which the premium is paid there shall be disregarded any guaranteed minimum pension to which the pensioner was entitled in connection with the employment to which the premium relates.
@ref sch 5 para 2(8) (src:5097)
GIVEN `a pensioner’s rights premium has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the increment falls to be paid after the date on which the premium is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weekly rate before the guaranteed minimum pension is disregarded` IS A NUMBER
      `the guaranteed minimum pension to which the pensioner was entitled in connection with the employment to which the premium relates` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para 2(8) the weekly rate used for an increment` MEANS
    IF `a pensioner’s rights premium has been paid` AND `the increment falls to be paid after the date on which the premium is paid`
    THEN JUST (`the weekly rate before the guaranteed minimum pension is disregarded` MINUS `the guaranteed minimum pension to which the pensioner was entitled in connection with the employment to which the premium relates`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a pensioner’s rights premium is paid ... after the date on which the premium is paid"

-- Paragraph 1 and 2 together: the increase of the pension for the deferment, for a person to whom paragraph 1 applies.
-- src:5080 | (1) This paragraph applies where a person’s entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred and one of the following conditions is met—
-- src:5081 | (a) the period of deferment is less than 12 months, or
-- src:5082 | (b) the person has made an election under paragraph A1(1)(a) in relation to the period of deferment.
-- src:5083 | (2) The rate of the person’s Category A or Category B retirement pension shall be increased by an amount equal to the aggregate of the increments to which he is entitled under paragraph 2, but only if that amount is enough to increase the rate of the pension by at least 1 per cent.
@ref sch 5 paras 1 and 2 (src:5080-5083)
GIVEN `the entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of deferment` IS A Period
      `the election made, or treated as made` IS A MAYBE `sch 5 Election`
      `the weekly rate to which the person would have been entitled for the period if the entitlement had not been deferred` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days in the period of deferment that regulations treat as days of increment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para 1 the amount by which the pension is increased for the deferment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 5 para 1(1) this paragraph applies` `the entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred` `the period of deferment` `the election made, or treated as made`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST (`sch 5 para 1(2) the amount by which the rate of the pension is increased` aggregate `the weekly rate to which the person would have been entitled for the period if the entitlement had not been deferred`)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 1(1) never answers FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 1(1) does not apply on these facts
    WHERE
        aggregate MEANS `sch 5 para 2 the aggregate of the increments` `the weekly rate to which the person would have been entitled for the period if the entitlement had not been deferred` `the number of days in the period of deferment that regulations treat as days of increment`

§§ `Paragraph 2A -- increase where the pension includes an increase under paragraphs 5 to 6A`

-- 2A(1): applies where deferred, the pension includes a paragraph 5 to 6A increase, and the (b) election made or treated.
-- src:5098 | (1) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:5099 | (a) a person’s entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred,
-- src:5100 | (b) the pension includes an increase under paragraphs 5 to 6A, and
-- src:5101 | (c) the person has made (or is treated as having made) an election under paragraph A1(1)(b) in relation to the period of deferment.
@ref sch 5 para 2A(1) (src:5098-5101)
GIVEN `the entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pension includes an increase under paragraphs 5 to 6A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the election made, or treated as made` IS A MAYBE `sch 5 Election`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 2A(1) this paragraph applies` MEANS
    IF `the entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred` AND `the pension includes an increase under paragraphs 5 to 6A` AND (`the election made, or treated as made` EQUALS JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 3A (the lump sum) applies`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph applies where ..." (a), (b) and (c)

-- 2A(3): the increment for each complete incremental period is 1/5th per cent of the weekly rate of the paragraphs 5 to 6A
-- increase. The text gives no rounding rule for this sub-paragraph (paragraph 2(4) is tied to paragraph 2(3)), so none is applied (NOTES.md, finding 26).
-- src:5103 | (3) For each complete incremental period in the person’s period of deferment, the amount of the increment shall be 1/5th per cent. of the weekly rate of the increase to which the person would have been entitled under paragraphs 5 to 6A for the period if his entitlement to the Category A or Category B retirement pension had not been deferred.
@ref sch 5 para 2A(3) (src:5103)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the increase under paragraphs 5 to 6A to which the person would have been entitled had the entitlement not been deferred` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 2A(3) the increment for one incremental period` MEANS
    (`the weekly rate of the increase under paragraphs 5 to 6A to which the person would have been entitled had the entitlement not been deferred` DIVIDED BY 5) DIVIDED BY 100

-- 2A(2): the rate is increased by the aggregate of those increments.
-- src:5102 | (2) The rate of the person’s Category A or Category B retirement pension shall be increased by an amount equal to the aggregate of the increments to which he is entitled under sub-paragraph (3).
@ref sch 5 para 2A(2) (src:5102)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the increase under paragraphs 5 to 6A to which the person would have been entitled had the entitlement not been deferred` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of complete incremental periods` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 2A(2) the amount by which the rate of the pension is increased` MEANS
    `the number of complete incremental periods`
    TIMES `sch 5 para 2A(3) the increment for one incremental period` `the weekly rate of the increase under paragraphs 5 to 6A to which the person would have been entitled had the entitlement not been deferred`

§§ `Paragraph 3 -- regulations on a change of rate during the deferment`

-- 3(1) and (2): regulation-making powers: inert (machinery) in NOTES.md.

§§ `Paragraph 3A -- lump sum where entitlement is deferred`

-- 3A(1) and (2): applies where deferred and the (b) election was made or is treated as made; the person is then entitled
-- to the lump sum of paragraph 3B.
-- src:5107 | (1) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:5108 | (a) a person’s entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred, and
-- src:5109 | (b) the person has made (or is treated as having made) an election under paragraph A1(1)(b) in relation to the period of deferment.
-- src:5110 | (2) The person is entitled to an amount calculated in accordance with paragraph 3B (a “lump sum”).
@ref sch 5 para 3A (src:5107-5110)
GIVEN `the entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the election made, or treated as made` IS A MAYBE `sch 5 Election`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 3A(2) the person is entitled to a lump sum` MEANS
    IF `the entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred` AND (`the election made, or treated as made` EQUALS JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 3A (the lump sum) applies`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph applies where ..." (a) and (b)

§§ `Paragraph 3B -- calculation of the lump sum`

-- 3B(2): "accrual period" means any period of seven days beginning with a prescribed day of the week, where that day
-- falls within the period of deferment. The prescribed day is an input, 0 = Sunday to 6 = Saturday (daydate's numbering).
-- src:5115 | ‘accrual period’ means any period of seven days beginning with a prescribed day of the week, where that day falls within the period of deferment.
@ref sch 5 para 3B(2) (src:5115)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday` IS A NUMBER
      `the period of deferment` IS A Period
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 3B(2) an accrual period begins on the day` MEANS
    (((Day day) MODULO 7) EQUALS `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday`)
    AND (day AT LEAST `the period of deferment`'s `the first day`)
    AND (day AT MOST `the period of deferment`'s `the last day`)

-- Helper for 3B(1), (2) and (4): how many days before (or on) a day the accrual period containing it began.
-- src:5115 | ‘accrual period’ means any period of seven days beginning with a prescribed day of the week, where that day falls within the period of deferment.
@ref sch 5 para 3B(2) (src:5115)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 3B(2) the days since the accrual period containing the day began` MEANS
    ((((Day day) MODULO 7) MINUS `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday`) PLUS 7) MODULO 7

-- 3B(1): the lump sum is the accrued amount for the LAST accrual period beginning during the period of deferment.
-- That period begins on the latest day of the prescribed weekday that is not after the last day of the deferment;
-- if none falls in the deferment, no accrual period begins during it and the text gives no lump sum (NOTHING).
-- src:5112 | (1) The lump sum is the accrued amount for the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment.
@ref sch 5 para 3B(1) (src:5112)
GIVEN `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday` IS A NUMBER
      `the period of deferment` IS A Period
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
`sch 5 para 3B(1) the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment` MEANS
    IF candidate AT LEAST `the period of deferment`'s `the first day`
    THEN JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS candidate, `the last day` IS candidate PLUS 6)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no accrual period begins during the period of deferment, and 3B(1) names only the last one
    WHERE
        lastDay MEANS `the period of deferment`'s `the last day`
        candidate MEANS lastDay MINUS (`sch 5 para 3B(2) the days since the accrual period containing the day began` lastDay `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday`)

-- 3B(3): the accrued amount for an accrual period is given by a formula (in A, P and R) that the converter omitted
-- from this text (the line is followed at once by "where--"). The encoding does not supply the formula from memory:
-- the function that would apply it answers NOTHING, and the amount is taken from the person's award figures where it is used.
-- 3B(2) defines "accrued amount" as the amount this sub-paragraph calculates, so the definition is cited here.
-- src:5113 | (2) In this paragraph—
-- src:5114 | ‘accrued amount’ means the amount calculated in accordance with sub-paragraph (3);
-- src:5116 | (3) The accrued amount for an accrual period for a person is—
-- src:5117 | where—
-- src:5118 | A is the accrued amount for the previous accrual period (or, in the case of the first accrual period beginning during the period of deferment, zero);
-- src:5119 | P is the amount of the Category A or Category B retirement pension to which the person would have been entitled for the accrual period if his entitlement had not been deferred;
@ref sch 5 para 3B(2) accrued amount, para 3B(3) (src:5113-5114) (src:5116-5119)
GIVEN `A, the accrued amount for the previous accrual period` IS A NUMBER
      `P, the amount of pension for the accrual period` IS A NUMBER
      `R, the percentage rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para 3B(3) the accrued amount for an accrual period` MEANS
    NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the formula that combines A, P and R is omitted from this text

-- 3B(3) "R": a percentage rate two per cent higher than the Bank of England base rate or, if regulations so provide,
-- such higher rate as may be prescribed. "two per cent higher" is read as two percentage points (NOTES.md, F4).
-- src:5120 | R is—
-- src:5121 | a percentage rate two per cent. higher than the Bank of England base rate, or
-- src:5122 | if regulations so provide, such higher rate as may be prescribed.
@ref sch 5 para 3B(3) R (src:5120-5122)
GIVEN `the Bank of England base rate, in per cent` IS A NUMBER
      `the higher rate prescribed by regulations, if they so provide` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para 3B(3) the percentage rate R` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the higher rate prescribed by regulations, if they so provide`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`the Bank of England base rate, in per cent` PLUS 2)
    WHEN JUST prescribed THEN
        IF prescribed GREATER THAN (`the Bank of England base rate, in per cent` PLUS 2)
        THEN JUST prescribed
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such higher rate as may be prescribed" names a rate higher than base rate plus two

-- 3B(4): a change in the base rate takes effect at the beginning of the accrual period immediately following the one in
-- which the change took effect, or at another time if regulations so provide.
-- src:5123 | (4) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (3), any change in the Bank of England base rate is to be treated as taking effect—
-- src:5124 | (a) at the beginning of the accrual period immediately following the accrual period during which the change took effect, or
-- src:5125 | (b) if regulations so provide, at such other time as may be prescribed.
@ref sch 5 para 3B(4) (src:5123-5125)
GIVEN `the day the change in the base rate took effect` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday` IS A NUMBER
      `the other time regulations provide, if they so provide` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 5 para 3B(4) the day a change in the base rate is treated as taking effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the other time regulations provide, if they so provide`
    WHEN JUST other THEN other
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        (`the day the change in the base rate took effect` MINUS (`sch 5 para 3B(2) the days since the accrual period containing the day began` `the day the change in the base rate took effect` `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday`)) PLUS 7

-- 3B(5)(a) and (b), (6): the amount of pension counted for an accrual period includes the section 47(1) increase
-- (read as in 2(6)) and the paragraph 4 increase; it does not include the section 83A or 85 increases, the paragraphs
-- 5 to 6A increases, graduated retirement benefit, or such other amount as is prescribed in prescribed circumstances.
-- src:5126 | (5) For the purposes of the calculation of the lump sum, the amount of Category A or Category B retirement pension to which the person would have been entitled for an accrual period—
-- src:5127 | (a) includes any increase under section 47(1) and any increase under paragraph 4 of this Schedule, but
-- src:5128 | (b) does not include—
-- src:5129 | (i) any increase under section 83A or 85 or paragraphs 5 to 6A of this Schedule,
-- src:5130 | (ii) any graduated retirement benefit, or
-- src:5131 | (iii) in prescribed circumstances, such other amount of Category A or Category B retirement pension as may be prescribed.
-- src:5132 | (6) The reference in sub-paragraph (5)(a) to any increase under subsection (1) of section 47 shall be taken as a reference to any increase that would take place under that subsection if subsection (2) of that section and section 46(5) of the Pensions Act were disregarded.
@ref sch 5 para 3B(5) and (6) (src:5126-5132)
GIVEN pension IS A `sch 5 Weekly pension`
      `the amount prescribed to be left out in prescribed circumstances` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 3B(5) the amount of pension counted for an accrual period` MEANS
    pension's `the pension apart from the increases named in this Schedule`
    PLUS pension's `the increase under section 47(1)`
    PLUS pension's `the increase under paragraph 4`
    MINUS `the amount prescribed to be left out in prescribed circumstances`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not include— (i) any increase under section 83A or 85 or paragraphs 5 to 6A of this Schedule, (ii) any graduated retirement benefit, or (iii) in prescribed circumstances, such other amount"

-- 3B(1) with the supplementary paragraph (7C(1)): the lump sum is the accrued amount for the last accrual period, rounded
-- to the nearest penny, 1/2p going to the next whole penny above. The accrued amount is an input because the formula is omitted.
-- src:5112 | (1) The lump sum is the accrued amount for the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment.
@ref sch 5 para 3B(1) (src:5112)
GIVEN `the accrued amount for the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para 3B(1) the lump sum before rounding` MEANS
    `the accrued amount for the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment`
